------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONVENTION IN FORCE (stated, NOT adjusted for)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Power-regime BACKWARD differences, A(n) = pi(b^n) - pi(b^(n-1)),
  with the primes 2 AND 3 EXCLUDED AS LATTICE, not counted as primes.
  A(1) = pi(b) - 2 for b >= 3; at b = 2 the two lattice primes straddle
  the regime boundary (2 in (1,2], 3 in (2,4]) so one is dropped from
  each of A(1) and A(2).   -- imported/lattice_mapper/README.md, Convention
  Nothing below adds them back.  Numbers here are therefore NOT comparable
  at low r with numbers in results/, which count 2 and 3 (CONTEXT.md).
  Cell (2,1) is convention-mobile (lab_notebook_2.md entry 47): its value
  moves with the seed rows, so its presence or absence below is a fact
  about the convention, not about cancellation.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE COORDINATE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  pair identity (lean/PairIdentity.lean, theorem pair_identity):
      prime(r,d) + composite(r,d) = (b-1)^(d+1) * b^(r-1-d)  =: total(b,r,d)
  scale       s(b,r,d) = (d+1)*log(b-1) + (r-1-d)*log b = log total
  normalised  nu(b,r,d) = |cell(r,d)| / total(b,r,d)     [exact Fraction]
  At b = 2, log(b-1) = 0 so s = (r-1-d)*log 2 and r-d alone fixes the
  scale -- PairIdentity.coeff_eq_one_iff_base_two.  At every other base
  both terms are live, so r, d and r-d are base-2 conveniences and the
  cross-base comparison is made in s.

